## Phase 1: Evidence-Backed Mechanism Extraction (`gta-anything extract`)

- [ ] Extract `GameplayIR` from authorized inputs (`spec.md`, `routes/*.xml`, or source repository):
  ```bash
  gta-anything --json extract {{SOURCE_PATH}} -o gameplay_ir.json --edition {{PRIMARY_EDITION}}
  ```
- [ ] Verify every core state, route/zone, and entity slot is backed by an `EvidenceAnchor` (`source_file`, `locator`, `extracted_fact`, `confidence`).

---

## Phase 2: World-Model Mapping & Vanilla-First Baseline (`gta-anything validate-ir`)

- [ ] Run static IR invariant validation:
  ```bash
  gta-anything --json validate-ir gameplay_ir.json
  ```
- [ ] Confirm all 5 hard invariants:
  - [ ] Every `EntitySlot` has a valid `vanilla_fallback_model` (e.g., `bus`, `airbus`, `mule`, `benson`).
  - [ ] `ui_spec.preview_mode` is `"static_sprite"` or `"static_metadata"` (**NEVER** `"live_3d_spawn"`).
  - [ ] All states in `state_machine` are reachable from `initial_state` (`Idle`).
  - [ ] Every `streaming`, `spawning`, `operation`, and `completion` state has a valid path to `cleanup_state` (`Teardown`).
  - [ ] Clean-room license is valid (`{{LICENSE}}`).

